Undo upstream 3d93fed0aab8 so the pre-fix defect of #15271 is present again.

This is a FIX REVERSAL on the pinned tree, not a parent build, and the case files
say so wherever they are quoted. It is the cleaner of the two for this row: only
the defect differs from the pin, where a backport to 2024 would also drag in two
years of unrelated change. It is only available because the fix is one hunk with no
second hardening elsewhere -- MPY-S02 and MPY-S03 were checked for the same
treatment and both failed it, see ../../STATUS.md.

Pre-fix, self->free is set to 8 BEFORE the allocation that is supposed to justify
it. If m_renew raises MemoryError the array is left claiming eight free slots it
does not own, and the next append writes past the end of the buffer.

--- w/py/objarray.c
+++ i/py/objarray.c
@@ -392,9 +392,8 @@ static mp_obj_t array_append(mp_obj_t self_in, mp_obj_t arg) {
     if (self->free == 0) {
         size_t item_sz = mp_binary_get_size('@', self->typecode, NULL);
         // TODO: alloc policy
-        size_t add_cnt = 8;
-        self->items = m_renew(byte, self->items, item_sz * self->len, item_sz * (self->len + add_cnt));
-        self->free = add_cnt;
+        self->free = 8;
+        self->items = m_renew(byte, self->items, item_sz * self->len, item_sz * (self->len + self->free));
         mp_seq_clear(self->items, self->len + 1, self->len + self->free, item_sz);
     }
